# M7.2 acceptance: saving settings restarts the sidecar with the new env.
#
# Run from the worktree root with an isolated HOME, an unreachable session bus
# (the key store is then reliably unavailable, so no key is stored), stray
# credentials in the app's own environment (spec item 1 must strip them), and
# the fake sidecar:
#
#   H=$(mktemp -d)
#   O=<repo>/.verify/m7.2/<impl|review|tester>
#   READER_SIDECAR_CMD="$PWD/tests/acceptance/m7.2-fake-sidecar.sh" \
#   READER_FAKE_LOG="$H/fake-sidecar.log" \
#     scripts/shot.sh -o "$O" -s tests/acceptance/m7.2.steps -- \
#     env HOME="$H" DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/nonexistent \
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-test-STRAYKEY0123456789 \
#     CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=stray-oauth-token \
#     ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=stray-auth-token \
#     ./build/app/agentic-reader
#   head -n 3 "$H/fake-sidecar.log"
#   grep -c '^start ' "$H/fake-sidecar.log"
#   tests/acceptance/m7.1-grep.sh "$H" "$O"
#
# Pass: shot.sh exits 0, every shot matches its comment, and
#   - head prints exactly these three lines, in this order (the first sidecar
#     got no credentials and no model; saving stopped it; the new one got the
#     saved model and, with the dev toggle on, no key):
#       start ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=unset CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=unset ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=unset READER_MODEL=unset
#       exit
#       start ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=unset CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=unset ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=unset READER_MODEL=claude-test-model
#   - grep -c prints 2 (Cancel restarts nothing),
#   - m7.1-grep.sh exits 0 (neither the stray key nor any key, both starting
#     "sk-ant-tes", reached a config, log, or screenshot dir).
#
# The fake sidecar (tests/acceptance/m7.2-fake-sidecar.sh) appends one "start"
# line per launch to $READER_FAKE_LOG naming which credential variables were
# set (never their values), waits 3 s, prints `ready`, and appends "exit" on
# stdin EOF.
#
# Not covered here: "Running replies are interrupted" needs a running reply,
# which the UI cannot start before the chat pane (M5.2) lands. The key path
# (dev toggle off with a stored key) needs a working secret service; the unit
# tests in tests/test_sidecar_env.cpp cover it.
#
# Assumptions (the spec is silent):
#   - The Preferences dialog is the M7.1 one, driven the same way: Alt+E, P
#     opens it with focus in the key field; Tab order is key field, Show,
#     Test key, model field, dev check box; Return in the model field is OK;
#     Escape cancels.
#   - "Settings changed, sidecar restarted" belongs in the chat pane (spec
#     item 5). The chat pane (M5.2) is not merged yet, so the status bar is
#     accepted instead. Once M5.2 is merged, either location passes.
#   - OK stops the running sidecar before it starts the new one. Cancel does
#     not restart it.
wait 5

# Main window, no dialog open. The status bar reads "Assistant ready": the
# first fake sidecar is up.
shot ready

key alt+e
wait 1
key p
wait 2
key Tab Tab Tab
type claude-test-model
key Tab
key space
wait 1

# The Preferences dialog is open: the model field reads "claude-test-model"
# and "Use my local Claude Code login (developer)" is checked.
shot prefs-edited

key shift+Tab
key Return
wait 1

# The dialog is closed, no message box is open, and the restarted fake
# sidecar is not ready yet (it waits 3 s). The text "Settings changed, sidecar
# restarted" is visible exactly, in the status bar (or, once M5.2 is merged,
# as a line in the chat pane). It does not read "Assistant ready" or
# "Assistant stopped, restarting..." and shows no error.
shot restarted

wait 5

# The restarted sidecar is up: the status bar reads "Assistant ready". No
# error dialog. If the restart message is in the chat pane, it is still there.
shot ready-again

key alt+e
wait 1
key p
wait 2

# The reopened dialog shows the saved settings: model "claude-test-model" and
# the dev check box checked.
shot reopened

key Escape
wait 5

# Cancel changed nothing: the dialog is closed, the status bar still reads
# "Assistant ready", and no new "Settings changed, sidecar restarted" message
# appeared (the chat pane, if present, shows the one from the earlier save
# only).
shot cancelled
